 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 5190,
   "ANSWER": "<p style=\"margin-left:24px; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>(i) Best-Suited Data Structure for the System</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:24px; text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The most suitable data structure for this task management system is a Stack because:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The system follows the Last In, First Out (LIFO) principle, where the most recently added task should be removed first.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The stack allows users to add a new task (push operation) and remove the most recent task (pop operation) efficiently.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Stacks are commonly used for undo operations, backtracking, and history tracking, making them ideal for a task management system where users may want to remove recent tasks first.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:24px; text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Example:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">A user adds Task 1, Task 2, and Task 3.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The system should store them in this order:<br />\n\tTop &rarr; Task 3 &rarr; Task 2 &rarr; Task 1 &rarr; Bottom</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">If the user removes a task, Task 3 (the most recent task) is removed first, which follows the LIFO principle.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:24px; text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Thus, a stack is the best choice for this task management system</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>(ii) Why Should the Stack Be Implemented Using a Linked List?</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Challenge of Using an Array-Based Stack</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">If we implement the stack using an array, the system will face a major issue:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Arrays require a fixed size. If the number of tasks grows beyond this limit, the array must be resized, which can slow down performance.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Memory may be wasted if fewer tasks are stored than the allocated size.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Since the task management system needs to handle an unlimited number of tasks, an array-based stack is not an efficient choice.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>How a Linked List-Based Stack Solves This Problem</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">A linked list-based stack does not require a fixed size because it allocates memory dynamically as tasks are added. Each task (node) consists of two parts:<br />\n1\ufe0f<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,sans-serif\">. </span>Data (task details).<br />\n2\ufe0f<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,sans-serif\">. P</span>ointer (link to the next task).</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>How It Works in the System:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>1.User Adding a Task (PUSH Operation):</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:24px; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Symbol\">&middot;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">&nbsp; A user enters a task name to add to the task stack.</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:24px; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Symbol\">&middot;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">&nbsp; A new node is created dynamically to store the task.</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:24px; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Symbol\">&middot;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">&nbsp; The new node is linked to the previous top task.</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:24px; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Symbol\">&middot;</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">&nbsp; The </span></span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">top</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"> pointer is updated to the newly added task.</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; When a new task is added, it is linked to the previous task and becomes the new top.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\">Pseudocode:</span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Function PUSH(task_name):</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Step 1: Create a new node</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; new_task = AllocateMemory()&nbsp; // Allocate memory for the new task</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Step 2: Store the task data</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; new_task.task_name = task_name&nbsp; // Assign task name to the new node</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Step 3: Link new task to the previous top</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; new_task.next = top&nbsp; // New task points to the old top task</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Step 4: Update the top pointer to new task</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; top = new_task&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Print &quot;Task added successfully: &quot;, task_name</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">End Function</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>2. User Removing the Most Recent Task (POP Operation):</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The system checks if the stack is empty before removing a task.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">If the stack is not empty:</span></span></span></span>\n\t<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The top task is removed.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The top pointer is updated to the next task in the stack.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">The removed task&rsquo;s memory is freed.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; When a task is removed, only the topmost node is deleted, without affecting other tasks.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Pseudocode</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Function POP():</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Step 1: Check if the stack is empty</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; If (top == NULL) Then</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Print &quot;No tasks to remove!&quot;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Return</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Step 2: Store the task being removed</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; removed_task = top.task_name&nbsp; // Store the task name for display</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Step 3: Move top pointer to the next task</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; temp = top&nbsp; // Store reference to current top task</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; top = top.next&nbsp; // Move top to the next node in the stack</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Step 4: Free memory of removed task</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; FreeMemory(temp)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Print &quot;Task removed: &quot;, removed_task</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">End Function</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\">&nbsp;</p>\n",
