   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p style=\"margin-left:24px; text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>A software developer is designing a web-based task management system where users can add, remove, and view the most recently added task first. The system must handle an unlimited number of tasks dynamically.</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-left:24px; text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>&nbsp;Based on this scenario, answer the following:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:lower-roman\">\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px; margin-left:8px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Which data structure is best suited for this system, and why?</b></span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-left:8px; text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Should the developer use an array-based stack or a linked list-based stack? Justify your answer with two reasons.</b></span></span></span></span></li>\n</ol>\n",
